  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Pantelija was given a sequence of positive integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​. Let's define the gcd value of this sequence as the number of its non-empty contiguous subsequences with greatest common divisor strictly greater than 111. The greatest common divisor of any contiguous subsequence al,al+1,…,ara_l, a_{l+1}, \\ldots, a_ral​,al+1​,…,ar​ (1≤l≤r≤N1 \\le l \\le r \\le N1≤l≤r≤N) is the greatest positive integer which divides each element of this subsequence.\n\nPantelija wants to maximise the gcd value of this sequence. In order to do that, he may choose a valid index iii, an integer bbb (1≤b≤5⋅1051 \\le b \\le 5 \\cdot 10^51≤b≤5⋅105, since he does not like large numbers) and change the element aia_iai​ to bbb. What is the maximum possible gcd value he can obtain?",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤5⋅1041 \\le N \\le 5 \\cdot 10^41≤N≤5⋅104",
      "1≤ai≤5⋅1051 \\le a_i \\le 5 \\cdot 10^51≤ai​≤5⋅105 for each valid iii",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (15 points):**",
      "1≤N≤1001 \\le N \\le 1001≤N≤100",
      "1≤ai≤1001 \\le a_i \\le 1001≤ai​≤100 for each valid iii",
      "**Subtask #2 (35 points):**",
      "1≤N≤5⋅1041 \\le N \\le 5 \\cdot 10^41≤N≤5⋅104",
      "1≤ai≤5001 \\le a_i \\le 5001≤ai​≤500 for each valid iii"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers a1,a2,…,aNa_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_Na1​,a2​,…,aN​.",
    "outputFormat": "Print a single line containing one integer ― the largest possible gcd value.",
    "notes": [],
